@startuml
!include ../shortfall/style.iuml

title Invalid input: edit-recipe 1 n/Changed p/-5
autonumber

actor User
participant "MishMash" as App
participant "parser: Parser" as Parser

User -> App : edit-recipe 1 n/Changed p/-5
App -> Parser : parseCommand(input)
activate Parser
note right of Parser : Dispatch to parseEditRecipe(arguments).
Parser -> Parser : parseRecipeIndex("1")
Parser --> Parser : 1
Parser -> Parser : collectRecipeArguments(prefixedFields, fields, ingredients)
note right of Parser
  Store n/Changed and p/-5 only in local fields.
  The original recipe has not been read or changed.
end note
Parser -> Parser : parseOptionalNutrition(fields, "p", "Protein")
activate Parser
Parser -> Parser : parseNutrition("-5", "Protein")
Parser --> Parser : throws IllegalArgumentException
deactivate Parser
note right of Parser
  parseEditRecipe catches the error and wraps it in
  MishMashException, retaining the cause and edit usage.
  The omitted calorie field is condensed here.
end note
Parser --> App : throws MishMashException
deactivate Parser
App -> App : displayError(exception)
App --> User : Error: Protein must be a non-negative integer.\nFollowed by edit-recipe usage.
note over App : executeCommand returns to the command-reading loop.
App -> App : displayCommandPrompt()
App --> User : Divider and next command prompt
User -> App : edit-recipe 1 p/55
ref over App, Parser
  The next command follows the normal successful parsing flow.
end ref

note over App, Parser
  No RecipeChanges, EditRecipeCommand, or replacement Recipe is created for the rejected input.
  The valid n/Changed field is not applied. Recipes, plans, and groceries remain unchanged.
end note
@enduml
